th cornwall england uk pub the seven stars is a grade ii listed public house in falmouth cornwall it was built in about 1800 and subsequently extended in 1912 to include an off-licence which later became a shop',datetime('now')),('Q18161693','The Old Ship','The Old Ship',51.4985,0.257908,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Old Ship, Aveley','the old ship public house in aveley essex england pub the old ship is a public house in aveley essex in england it is on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors',datetime('now')),('Q18161702','The Shakespeare','The Shakespeare',53.550027,-2.403438,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Shakespeare, Farnworth','the shakespeare pub in farnworth greater manchester england uk pub the shakespeare is a grade ii listed former public house on glynne street in farnworth a town in the metropolitan borough of bolton greater manchester england built in 1926 for magee marshall & co and reputedly rebuilt following a fire it was designed with a distinctive calendar theme expressed through its external features',datetime('now')),('Q18161793','The Pheasant Inn','The Pheasant Inn',54.66486,-3.24197,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Pheasant Inn, Bassenthwaite','the pheasant inn pub in wythop cumbria united kingdom pub the pheasant inn is a historic coaching inn and public house in the civil parish of wythop near bassenthwaite lake cumbria in the english lake district it dates from the 18th century and is grade ii listed',datetime('now')),('Q18161900','Square and Compass','Square and Compass',50.597905,-2.037149,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Square and Compass, Worth Matravers','square and compass pub in worth matravers dorset england uk pub the square and compass is a grade ii listed public house in worth matravers dorset built in the 18th century as a pair of cottages before becoming a public house the square and compass got its name in 1830 from a landlord who had been a stonemason',datetime('now')),('Q18161920','Queen''s Head','Queen''s Head',51.7737,0.796449,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Queen''s Head, Tolleshunt D''Arcy','queen''s head pub in tolleshunt d''arcy pub the queen''s head is a public house at the square tolleshunt d''arcy essex it has been there since at least 1899',datetime('now')),('Q18162102','Sun and 13 Cantons','Sun and 13 Cantons',51.5127,-0.136603,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Sun and 13 Cantons','sun and 13 cantons pub in westminster london england uk pub the sun and 13 cantons is a grade ii listed public house at 20 great pulteney street soho london w1 the pub which takes its name from swiss woollen merchants who used to be based nearby has operated on this site since at least 1756',datetime('now')),('Q18162138','The Swan','The Swan',51.644483,-0.803449,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Swan, West Wycombe','the swan pub in west wycombe buckinghamshire england uk pub the swan is a grade ii listed pub at high street west wycombe buckinghamshire it is on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors',datetime('now')),('Q18162256','The Magdala','The Magdala',51.5556,-0.1656,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Magdala','the magdala pub in hampstead london uk pub the magdala also known as the magdala tavern or colloquially as simply the magy is a pub on south hill park in hampstead north london named after the british victory in the 1868 battle of magdala it was the site of the murder of david blakely by ruth ellis in 1955',datetime('now')),('Q18162259','The Morning Star','The Morning Star',53.113351,-3.31366,'GB','pub',1639,22.85,'The Morning Star, Ruthin','the morning star pub in ruthin denbighshire wales pub the morning star or the star inn ruthin was listed as a grade ii building on 16 may 1978 it is directly opposite the ruthin gaol and is claimed to be the oldest pub in ruthin',datetime('now')),('Q18162320','Three Horseshoes','Three Horseshoes',52.740027,-1.353046,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Three Horseshoes, Whitwick','three horseshoes pub in whitwick leicestershire england uk pub the three horseshoes is a grade ii listed public house at 11 leicester road whitwick leicestershire le67 5gn it is on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors it was originally two cottages built in the early mid 19th century converted and extended with a front range to create pub in 1882',datetime('now')),('Q18162323','The Three Stags'' Heads','The Three Stags'' Heads',53.2772,-1.72999,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Three Stags'' Heads','the three stags'' heads pub in wardlow derbyshire england uk pub farmhouse the three stags'' heads is a grade ii listed public house in wardlow mires derbyshire england on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors it was built in the mid late 18th century with 19th- and 20th-century alterations and additions',datetime('now')),('Q18162377','Travellers Rest','Travellers Rest',53.1344,-2.6322,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Travellers Rest, Alpraham','travellers rest pub in alpraham cheshire pub the travellers rest is a public house at alpraham near tarporley in cheshire england it is on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors',datetime('now')),('Q18162495','The Victoria','The Victoria',54.772064,-1.570433,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Victoria, Durham','the victoria pub in durham england uk pub hotel the victoria is a grade ii listed public house at 86 hallgarth street durham dh1 3as it was built in 1899 by the newcastle architect joseph oswald it is on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors',datetime('now')),('Q18162502','The Victoria','The Victoria',53.781351,-2.40496,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Victoria, Great Harwood','the victoria pub in great harwood lancashire england uk pub the victoria is a grade ii listed public house at st john''s street great harwood blackburn lancashire bb6 7ep it is on the campaign for real ale''s national inventory of historic pub interiors it was built in 1905',datetime('now')),('Q18162520','Stanley Arms','Stanley Arms',53.4816,-2.35704,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Stanley Arms, Eccles','stanley arms pub in eccles greater manchester england uk pub the stanley arms is a grade ii listed public house on liverpool road in patricroft a suburb near the market town of eccles in the city of salford england built in the late 19th century it has been a joseph holt pub since 1910 when alterations are understood to have been made and a neighbouring terraced house was incorporated',datetime('now')),('Q18162674','The Wheatsheaf, Fitzrovia','The Wheatsheaf, Fitzrovia',51.517747,-0.134025,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Wheatsheaf, Fitzrovia','the wheatsheaf fitzrovia public house in camden london pub the wheatsheaf is a pub in rathbone place fitzrovia london that was popular with london''s bohemian set in the 1930s its customers included george orwell dylan thomas edwin muir and humphrey jennings who were known for a while as the wheatsheaf writers other habitués included the singer and dancer betty may and the writer and surrealist poet philip o''connor nina hamnett julian maclaren-ross anthony carson and quentin crisp',datetime('now')),('Q18162682','White Lion, Barthomley','White Lion, Barthomley',53.0686,-2.3482,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'White Lion, Barthomley','white lion barthomley grade ii listed public house in barthomley cheshire england uk thatched pub the white lion is a public house in barthomley cheshire england just off junction 16 of the m6 it was built in 1614 and is recorded in the national heritage list for england as a designated grade ii listed building',datetime('now')),('Q18162741','The Winchester, Highgate','The Winchester, Highgate',51.5735,-0.1408,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Winchester, Highgate','the winchester highgate pub in haringey london england uk pub the winchester is a public house in highgate london it was built in 1881 as the winchester tavern and later became the winchester hall hotel',datetime('now')),('Q18162967','The Vine, Pamphill','The Vine, Pamphill',