e('now')),('Q26320031','Bakers Vaults Public House','Bakers Vaults Public House',53.411894,-2.157321,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Bakers Vaults','bakers vaults public house grade ii listed pub in stockport greater manchester england uk pub bakers vaults is a grade ii listed public house on market place stockport greater manchester england built in the late 19th century it stands on the site of the former george and dragon inn which dated from around 1775 and occupied the surviving foundations of stockport castle',datetime('now')),('Q26320038','The Kings Arms Public House','The Kings Arms Public House',53.411983,-2.157547,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'King''s Arms, Stockport','the kings arms public house grade ii listed pub in stockport greater manchester england uk pub the king''s arms is a grade ii listed former public house on bridge street brow in stockport greater manchester england built in the early to mid-19th century it is thought to have replaced an earlier inn called the greyhound',datetime('now')),('Q26320048','Star and Garter public house','Star and Garter public house',53.403173,-2.152975,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Star and Garter, Stockport','star and garter public house grade ii listed pub in stockport greater manchester england uk pub the star and garter is a grade ii listed public house on higher hillgate in stockport greater manchester england built in the early 19th century it was originally a hotel before later becoming a pub',datetime('now')),('Q26320062','Two Tubbs','Two Tubbs',53.594,-2.297912,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Two Tubs','two tubbs pub in bury greater manchester england uk pub the two tubs is a grade ii listed public house on the wylde in bury greater manchester england probably built in the late 17th century it was converted from a private residence into a pub in 1806 and was then known as the globe inn',datetime('now')),('Q26320076','The Bank','The Bank',53.592959,-2.297699,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Bank, Bury','the bank pub in bury greater manchester england uk pub the bank officially listed as 18 and 20 market street is a grade ii listed public house on market street in bury greater manchester england built around 1860 1870 as a branch of the manchester and district bank it continued to appear as a bank on early 20th century ordnance survey maps',datetime('now')),('Q26320087','Church Inn','Church Inn',53.529808,-2.286183,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Church Inn','church inn pub in prestwich bury greater manchester england uk pub the church inn is a grade ii listed public house on church lane in prestwich a town within the metropolitan borough of bury greater manchester england historic england describes it as an 18th century building while the campaign for real ale camra notes earlier origins and gives 1629 as the earliest known date',datetime('now')),('Q26320107','Shoulder of Mutton','Shoulder of Mutton',53.645775,-2.331351,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Shoulder of Mutton, Holcombe','shoulder of mutton pub in holcombe bury greater manchester england uk pub the shoulder of mutton is a grade ii listed public house on holcombe village in holcombe a village within the metropolitan borough of bury greater manchester england built in the late 18th century on the site of an earlier inn it was damaged during an airship raid in 1916',datetime('now')),('Q26320149','Blundell Arms','Blundell Arms',53.595305,-2.506207,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Blundell Arms','blundell arms pub in horwich bolton greater manchester england uk pub the blundell arms is a grade ii listed public house on chorley old road in horwich a town on the edge of the west pennine moors in the metropolitan borough of bolton greater manchester england the building has 17th century origins with early 19th century work',datetime('now')),('Q26320299','White Horse Public House','White Horse Public House',53.503031,-2.359348,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'White Horse, Swinton','white horse public house pub in swinton greater manchester england uk pub the white horse is a grade ii listed public house on worsley road in swinton a town in the city of salford england built in the mid to late 18th century and partly rebuilt in the 20th century it is regarded by the campaign for real ale camra as the oldest pub in swinton',datetime('now')),('Q26320324','Queens Arms','Queens Arms',53.484976,-2.358574,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Queen''s Arms, Patricroft','queens arms pub in salford greater manchester england uk pub the queen''s arms is a grade ii listed public house on green lane in patricroft a suburb near the market town of eccles in the city of salford england built in 1828 as an early refreshment stop for the liverpool and manchester railway described as laying claim to being the world''s first railway pub it was renamed the queen''s arms after queen victoria''s 1851 visit to salford and is rated by the campaign for real ale camra with two stars for having an interior of very special national historic interest',datetime('now')),('Q26320740','Old Market Tavern','Old Market Tavern|Antiguo ayuntamiento de Altrincham',53.389263,-2.35054,'GB','pub',NULL,19.85,'Old Town Hall, Altrincham','old market tavern pub in altrincham trafford greater manchester england uk pub city hall hotel the old town hall officially listed as old market tavern is a grade ii listed former municipal building on old market place in altrincham a market town in trafford greater manchester england the listing records the complex as an early 19th century hotel incorporating the former town hall of 1849 originally a separate civic building that served as the headquarters of the old borough of altrincham until the late 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26320785','Stamford Arms','Stamford Arms',53.508971,-2.028595,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Stamford Arms','stamford arms pub in tameside greater manchester england uk pub the stamford arms is a grade ii listed public house on huddersfield road in carrbrook a village east of stalybridge in tameside greater manchester england built in the mid-18th 