nsion at the rear and two 20th century additions to either side',datetime('now')),('Q26456505','Boar''s Head','Boar''s Head',53.412047,-2.15678,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Boar''s Head, Stockport','boar''s head grade ii listed pub in stockport greater manchester england uk pub the boar''s head officially listed as the boars head hotel is a grade ii listed former public house on the corner of vernon street and market place stockport greater manchester england built in the early 19th century it received a new frontage to market place later in the century',datetime('now')),('Q26456712','Boar''s Head Public House','Boar''s Head Public House',53.49821,-2.518665,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Boar''s Head, Leigh','boar''s head public house grade ii listed pub in leigh wigan greater manchester wn7 pub the boar''s head is a grade ii listed public house on market place in leigh a town within the metropolitan borough of wigan greater manchester england built in 1900 to designs by local architect christopher simpson for the leigh brewery it replaced an earlier pub on the same site and incorporates a former stable block that is also listed at grade ii the building retains notable historic features and its interior is recognised by the campaign for real ale camra with a one star rating for its special national h',datetime('now')),('Q26457511','The Grapes','The Grapes',53.842771,-0.431975,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Grapes, Beverley','the grapes pub in beverley east riding of yorkshire england uk pub the grapes is a historic pub in beverley a town in the east riding of yorkshire in england the building on saturday market was constructed in about 1751 when it was granted an alcohol licence',datetime('now')),('Q26457588','Duke William Inn','Duke William Inn',53.588788,-2.359804,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Duke William Inn','duke william inn pub in bury greater manchester england uk pub inn the duke william inn is a grade ii listed public house on well street in ainsworth a village near radcliffe within the metropolitan borough of bury greater manchester england although dated 1737 it was likely a remodel of an older building and has been subsequently changed',datetime('now')),('Q26458558','The Queens Head Public House','The Queens Head Public House',52.124622,0.099493,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Queen''s Head, Newton','the queens head public house pub in newton south cambridgeshire england uk pub the queen''s head is a pub in newton cambridgeshire england it is grade ii listed and has been a pub since 1729',datetime('now')),('Q26461272','The Foords Hotel','The Foords Hotel',54.210645,-0.285843,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Foords Hotel','the foords hotel hotel in filey scarborough north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the foords hotel is a historic public house on queen street in filey a town in north yorkshire england the building was constructed in about 1815 to serve early visitors to the seaside resort',datetime('now')),('Q26468118','The Red Lion Hotel','The Red Lion Hotel',51.766675,-0.214812,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Red Lion, Hatfield','the red lion hotel pub in hatfield welwyn hatfield hertfordshire england uk pub the red lion is a grade ii listed public house and former hotel on the great north road hatfield in hertfordshire the building dates from the late eighteenth century with nineteenth century additions and a large 1950s rear extension',datetime('now')),('Q26468567','The Ship Inn','The Ship Inn',54.092578,-1.380614,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Ship Inn, Aldborough','the ship inn grade ii listed pub in aldborough north yorkshire england uk pub inn the ship inn is a grade ii listed public house in aldborough north yorkshire england between 2008 and november 2024 the pub was owned by brian rey and elaine howden who came to prominence after gordon ramsay visited their previous pub the fenwick arms in claughton lancashire in a 2006 episode of ramsay''s kitchen nightmares',datetime('now')),('Q26468691','George and Dragon','George and Dragon',54.269733,-0.931877,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'George and Dragon, Kirkbymoorside','george and dragon inn in kirkbymoorside north yorkshire england uk pub the george and dragon is a historic pub on market place in kirkbymoorside a town in north yorkshire england the building was originally a medieval cruck framed structure',datetime('now')),('Q26468750','The Eclipse Inn','The Eclipse Inn',51.062181,-1.314858,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Eclipse Inn','the eclipse inn pub in winchester hampshire england uk pub inn the eclipse inn is a public house at 25 the square in the city of winchester in hampshire england it has been listed grade ii on the national heritage list for england nhle since january 1974',datetime('now')),('Q26468792','Punch Bowl Inn','Punch Bowl Inn',54.060841,-1.363058,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Punch Bowl Inn, Marton cum Grafton','punch bowl inn pub in marton cum grafton harrogate north yorkshire england uk pub inn the punch bowl inn is a historic public house on main street in marton cum grafton a village in north yorkshire england the building is thought to have originally been constructed in the late 16th century probably as a two-bay house this oldest section is timber framed',datetime('now'));
