s Arms Inn',54.257572,-1.897933,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Foresters Arms','foresters arms inn pub in carlton town richmondshire north yorkshire england uk pub inn the foresters arms is a historic pub on village street in carlton a village in coverdale north yorkshire england the building was constructed in the 17th century as a single-roomed farmhouse',datetime('now')),('Q26474307','The Godwins','The Godwins',52.067464,-2.642706,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Godwins Hotel, Bartestree','the godwins inn in lugwardine herefordshire england uk hotel inn the godwins hotel in bartestree herefordshire england is a building of historical significance and is grade ii listed on the english heritage register it was built in 1879 by william henry godwin the owner of the famous tile manufacturing firm of messrs william godwin and sons',datetime('now')),('Q26474690','Kings Head Inn','Kings Head Inn',54.379205,-2.076466,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'King''s Head, Gunnerside','kings head inn pub in melbecks richmondshire north yorkshire england uk pub inn the king''s head is a pub in gunnerside a village in north yorkshire in england the pub was built in 1760',datetime('now')),('Q26479963','Sir Ralph Abercromby','Sir Ralph Abercromby',53.4785,-2.2478,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Sir Ralph Abercromby (pub)','sir ralph abercromby pub in manchester pub the sir ralph abercromby also known as the abercrombie is a pub between jackson''s row and bootle street in manchester england named after lieutenant-general sir ralph abercromby built in the 19th century it is one of the few structures remaining in the area from the time of the peterloo massacre',datetime('now')),('Q26482318','Egerton Arms','Egerton Arms',53.621345,-2.227372,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Egerton Arms','egerton arms pub in rochdale greater manchester england uk pub the egerton arms is a grade ii listed former public house on chapel lane in ashworth a hamlet within the metropolitan borough of rochdale greater manchester england built in the early to mid-18th century it is reported to have closed in 2004 and was later converted to residential use',datetime('now')),('Q26483787','The Three Tuns Inn','The Three Tuns Inn',54.368191,-1.299024,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Three Tuns, Osmotherley','the three tuns inn pub in osmotherley north yorkshire england uk pub inn the three tuns is a historic pub in osmotherley north yorkshire a village in england the pub was built in the 17th century and the building was altered early in the 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26484021','Fallow Buck Inn','Fallow Buck Inn',51.672746,-0.09368,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Fallow Buck Inn','fallow buck inn pub in clay hill london pub inn the fallow buck inn is a public house in clay hill enfield and a grade ii listed building with historic england',datetime('now')),('Q26484055','The Cleveland Tontine Inn','The Cleveland Tontine Inn',54.387326,-1.317993,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Cleveland Tontine','the cleveland tontine inn inn in ingleby arncliffe hambleton north yorkshire england uk hotel inn the cleveland tontine is a historic building in ingleby arncliffe a village in north yorkshire in england in the early 19th century a turnpike was constructed from crathorne to join the existing road from thirsk to stokesley',datetime('now')),('Q26484769','Hales Bars','Hales Bars',53.993925,-1.54671,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Hales Bar','hales bars pub in harrogate north yorkshire england uk pub hales bar is a pub in harrogate a town in north yorkshire in england the promenade inn one of the first in the town opened before 1766 when tobias smollett visited later setting scenes in his novel the expedition of humphry clinker in the pub',datetime('now')),('Q26485559','Mother Shipton Inn','Mother Shipton Inn',54.002939,-1.467884,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Mother Shipton Inn','mother shipton inn pub in knaresborough harrogate north yorkshire england uk pub inn the mother shipton inn is a historic pub in knaresborough a town in north yorkshire in england the building was constructed in the 17th century to serve as a gatehouse for the long walk promenade',datetime('now')),('Q26486107','Dean''s Place Hotel','Dean''s Place Hotel',50.805159,0.155404,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Dean''s Place Hotel','dean''s place hotel country house hotel in alfriston wealden east sussex england uk pub country house hotel dean''s place in alfriston east sussex is a building of historical significance and is a grade ii listed building it was built in the 17th century or earlier and was the residence of several notable people over the next three hundred years',datetime('now')),('Q26486682','Simpson''s Tavern','Simpson''s Tavern',51.513022,-0.085948,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Simpson''s Tavern','simpson''s tavern pub in city of london england uk pub simpson''s tavern was a pub and restaurant at 38 1 2 ball court alley cornhill in the city of london ec3 simpson''s occupied a grade ii listed building built in the late 17th and early 18th centuries',datetime('now')),('Q26487354','The Old Bank of England','The Old Bank of England|オールド・バンク・オブ・イングランド',51.513932,-0.111488,'GB','pub',NULL,24.64,'The Old Bank of England','the old bank of england pub in fleet street london pub the old bank of england is a public house at 194 fleet street where the city of london meets the city of westminster it was constructed on a corner site in 1886 by sir arthur blomfield in a grand italianate style the interior having three large chandeliers with a detailed plaster ceiling',datetime('now')),('Q26487647','The Ship, Hart Street','The Ship, Hart Street|The Ship (Rua Hart)',51.510896,-0.079939,'GB','pub',1887,22.85,'The Ship, Hart Street','the ship hart street pub at 3 hart street aldgate london ec3r pub the ship is a victorian-era pub at 3 hart street aldgate london ec3 it is a grade ii listed building built in 1887',datetime('now')),('Q26488103','The Ship','The Ship',51.512019,-0.083478,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Ship Tavern, Lime Street','the ship pub in lime street city of london pub the ship was a pub at 27 lime street london ec3 the building is a grade ii listed building built in the mid-19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26489064','The Crown Inn Public House','The Crown Inn Public House',51.603929,-0.954899,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Crown Inn, Pishill','the crown inn public house pub in pishill with stonor south oxfordshire england uk pub the crown inn was a pub in the south oxfordshire village of pishill near henley-on-thames it dates from the 17th century',datetime('now')),('Q26489084','The Cockpit','The Cockpit',51.512702,-0.101509,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Cockpit, City of London','the cockpit pub in the city of london pub the cockpit is a circa 1860 pub on st andrew''s hill in the city of london where it meets ireland yard formerly named the cock pit having hosted cockfights it became the three castles in the mid-19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26489533','Greaves Park','Greaves Park',54.040819,-2.794538,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Greaves Park','greaves park pub in lancaster lancashire england uk pub greaves house now known as greaves park is a grade ii listed house in lancaster england now a pub and restaurant and is also the name of the surrounding public park it was built in 1843 by the reverend samuel simpson and was the residence of many notable people for the next century',datetime('now')),('Q26492204','The Churchill Public House','The Churchill Public House',53.477766,-2.23608,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Churchill, Manchester','the churchill public house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the churchill formerly known as the mechanics arms and churchills and now trading as the church is a grade ii listed public house on chorlton street adjacent to canal street in manchester england within the city''s gay village it is one of the area''s oldest venues having operated as a pub since the 1850s and later functioning as a hotel drag and karaoke venue',datetime('now')),('Q26492372','City Arms Public House','City Arms Public House',53.479322,-2.242887,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'City Arms','city arms public house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the city arms is a grade ii listed public house on kennedy street in manchester england it is housed within a former late 18th century townhouse that once formed part of a small terrace',datetime('now')),('Q26493956','The Bruce Arms Inn','The Bruce Arms Inn',54.204875,-1.589434,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Bruce Arms','the bruce arms inn pub in west tanfield hambleton north yorkshire england uk pub inn the bruce arms is a historic pub on main street in west tanfield a village in north yorkshire england the coaching inn and its stables were built in the early 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26494042','The Golden Lion','The Golden Lion',54.339184,-1.433604,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Golden Lion Hotel, Northallerton','the golden lion pub in northallerton hambleton north yorkshire england uk pub the golden lion hotel is a historic building in northallerton a town in north yorkshire in england the original golden lion was a small coaching inn built in the 18th century the third to be established in the town after the black bull and the king''s head',datetime('now')),('Q26495034','The Rattlebone Inn','The Rattlebone Inn',51.572278,-2.212264,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Rattlebone Inn','the rattlebone inn inn in sherston wiltshire england uk inn the rattlebone inn is a public house in sherston wiltshire england it has been listed grade ii on the national heritage list for england since december 1986',datetime('now')),('Q2649692','Mutters','Mutters|Nockhof',47.2183,11.3574,'AT','pub',NULL,19.02,NULL,'mutters building in mutters austria mountain hut inn',datetime('now')),('Q26497418','The Spotted Cow Public House','The Spotted Cow Public House',54.136126,-0.800334,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Spotted Cow, Malton','the spotted cow public house pub in malton ryedale north yorkshire england uk pub the spotted cow is a historic pub in malton north yorkshire a town in england the age of the building is uncertain historic england describes it as being 18th century or possibly earlier while the gazette and herald describes it as being 16th century',datetime('now')),('Q26502441','The Guild','The Guild',53.764357,-2.711273,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Guild, Preston','the guild pub in preston lancashire england uk pub house the guild is a grade ii listed public house at 99 fylde road in preston lancashire england it was built as the home of the cotton manufacturer william taylor and became a pub in the late 1980s',datetime('now')),('Q26507407','Crab Inn','Crab Inn',50.62578,-1.178222,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Crab, Shanklin','crab inn pub in shanklin isle of wight england uk thatched pub the crab is a pub in shanklin on the isle of wight off the south coast of the uk located in the old village above the beach as a traditional thatched building surrounded by other old buildings it has often been photographed and painted the shanklin and district history society describe it as possibly the most drawn painted and photographed building on the island and camra''s notes on the pub comment that it has adorned many a chocolate box as of 2026 it is operated by greene king and has been a grade ii listed building since 1992',datetime('now')),('Q26510567','The Parrot And Punchbowl Public House','The Parrot And Punchbowl Public House',52.193197,1.577334,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Parrot and Punchbowl, Aldringham','the parrot and punchbowl public house pub in aldringham cum thorpe suffolk coastal suffolk england uk pub the parrot and punchbowl is a 16th-century english pub in the suffolk village of aldringham in the aldringham-cum-thorpe parish it is a grade ii listed building associated with a history of smuggling',datetime('now')),('Q26511320','The Swan Inn, Worlingworth','The Swan Inn, Worlingworth',52.26738,1.258118,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Swan Inn, Worlingworth','the swan inn worlingworth pub in worlingworth mid suffolk england uk thatched pub pub the swan inn is a public house in the village of worlingworth suffolk england it is a grade ii listed building',datetime('now')),('Q26511883','The Hare And Hounds Public House','The Hare And Hounds Public House',52.434617,-1.893081,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Hare & Hounds, Kings Heath','the hare and hounds public house pub in birmingham west midlands england uk pub the hare & hounds occasionally and commonly referred to as the hare and hounds is a public house and music venue on the high street in the kings heath area of birmingham england originally built in 1820 and remodelled to its current form in 1907 the hare & hounds is grade ii listed as it retains many original art nouveau internal fixtures',datetime('now')),('Q26515014','The Gate Public House','The Gate Public House',54.13473,-0.797298,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Gate, Malton','the gate public house pub in malton ryedale north yorkshire england uk pub the gate is a historic closed pub in malton north yorkshire a town in england the building lies on yorkersgate and was originally two houses',datetime('now')),('Q26515023','20 and 22, The Broadway','20 and 22, The Broadway',51.405863,-1.324882,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'George and Pelican Inn','20 and 22 the broadway building in newbury west berkshire england uk coaching inn the george and pelican inn was an english coaching inn that provided food entertainment and overnight accommodation for travellers between london and bath for over 200 years from the middle of the seventeenth century until the opening of newbury station in 1847 originally two separate inns they later combined although each retained a separate identity by providing different services',datetime('now')),('Q26515257','The Fighting Cocks Public House','The Fighting Cocks Public House',52.447045,-1.887769,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Fighting Cocks, Moseley','the fighting cocks public house pub in birmingham west midlands england uk pub the fighting cocks is a grade ii listed public house in moseley birmingham england',datetime('now')),('Q2651633','Altes Brauhaus','Altes Brauhaus',49.375473,10.181282,'DE','brewery',NULL,19.85,'Altes Brauhaus (Rothenburg ob der Tauber)','altes brauhaus historical building brewery the altes brauhaus is an historic building in the centre of rothenburg ob der tauber in bavaria southern germany it was originally a brewery',datetime('now')),('Q2651916','Den Groenen Staek','Den Groenen Staek',51.081667,3.688333,'BE','pub',NULL,13.17,NULL,'den groenen staek protected townscape inn',datetime('now'));
