ia inn is a public house and inn in the english village of elterwater cumbria dating to the 17th century it is a grade ii listed building',datetime('now')),('Q26538144','The Tall Ships Public House','The Tall Ships Public House',51.861679,-2.250326,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Tall Ship, Gloucester','the tall ships public house pub in gloucester gloucestershire england uk pub the tall ship is a grade ii listed building at 134 southgate street gloucester it is located at the entrance to gloucester docks',datetime('now')),('Q26538407','The Three Horse Shoes Public House','The Three Horse Shoes Public House',54.09672,-1.396128,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Tap on the Tutt','the three horse shoes public house pub in boroughbridge harrogate north yorkshire england uk pub the tap on the tutt is a historic pub on bridge street in boroughbridge a town in north yorkshire england the pub was commissioned by hepworth & co a brewer based in ripon for a site on the great north road',datetime('now')),('Q26538701','Crown And Kettle Public House','Crown And Kettle Public House',53.484776,-2.232382,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Crown and Kettle','crown and kettle public house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the crown and kettle is a grade ii listed public house on the corner of oldham road and great ancoats street in the ancoats area of manchester england dating from around 1800 and originally known as the iron dish & cob of coal it stands on a site recorded as early as 1734',datetime('now')),('Q26539307','Nos 74-78, and No 80 (The Grey Horse Public House) and Attached Railings, Portland Street','Nos 74-78, and No 80 (The Grey Horse Public House) and Attached Railings, Portland Street',53.477903,-2.239938,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'74–80 Portland Street','nos 74-78 and no 80 the grey horse public house and attached railings portland street pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub 74 80 portland street is a grade ii listed terrace of four late-18th century former townhouses now commercial buildings on portland street in manchester city centre england no',datetime('now')),('Q26539404','Circus Tavern','Circus Tavern',53.47783,-2.240043,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Circus Tavern, Manchester','circus tavern pub in manchester england pub the circus tavern is a grade ii listed public house on portland street in manchester england originally built as a house in the late 18th or early 19th century it was later extended and converted into a pub becoming established in that role by about 1840',datetime('now')),('Q26539756','New Union Public House','New Union Public House',53.476347,-2.238374,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'New Union, Manchester','new union public house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the new union formerly known as the union hotel is a grade ii listed public house and hotel on princess street adjacent to canal street in manchester england within the city''s gay village established in the 1860s it is one of the area''s longest standing venues and operates as a drag and karaoke venue as well as a hotel',datetime('now')),('Q26539905','Marble Arch Inn','Marble Arch Inn',53.488344,-2.232507,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Marble Arch Inn','marble arch inn pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the marble arch inn is a grade ii listed public house on rochdale road in the ancoats area of manchester england designed by darbyshire & smith and built in 1888 on the site of an earlier mckenna''s brewery show house it retains a richly detailed victorian interior recognised by the campaign for real ale camra as being of outstanding national historic importance',datetime('now')),('Q26544567','Marton Arms Inn','Marton Arms Inn',54.157423,-2.483491,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Marton Arms Hotel','marton arms inn pub in thornton in lonsdale craven north yorkshire england uk pub inn the marton arms hotel is a historic pub in thornton in lonsdale a village in north yorkshire in england the inn was built in 1679 and was altered in the 19th and 20th centuries',datetime('now')),('Q26546503','Queen of Hearts','Queen of Hearts',53.443005,-2.21895,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Queen of Hearts, Manchester','queen of hearts pub in manchester greater manchester england uk school building pub the queen of hearts now trading as 256 wilmslow road is a grade ii listed building on wilmslow road in fallowfield an area of manchester england designed by price and linklater in the gothic style and built between 1870 and 1872 for the church of the holy innocents as a school it was later converted into a public house receiving its listing while serving that role and now operates as a bar and venue',datetime('now')),('Q26546572','Ye Olde Cock Inn','Ye Olde Cock Inn',53.410596,-2.231119,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Ye Olde Cock Inn','ye olde cock inn pub in didsbury manchester greater manchester england uk pub inn ye olde cock inn is a grade ii listed public house on wilmslow road in didsbury a suburb of manchester england built in the late 18th century as an inn it has had varied uses including a period as a seafood restaurant before being returned to pub restaurant use by greene king in 2011',datetime('now')),('Q26546631','Withington Ale House','Withington Ale House',53.433475,-2.229257,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'White Lion, Withington','withington ale house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the white lion is a grade ii listed former public house on wilmslow road in withington a suburb of manchester england designed by the architect william mellor in the eclectic gothic style and built in 1881 it operated as a tied house and remained in use until its closure in 2005',datetime('now')),('Q26546774','Old Angel Public House','Old Angel Public House',52.953365,-1.143454,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Old Angel Inn','old angel public house building in nottingham nottinghamshire england uk pub the old angel inn is a grade ii listed public house in the lace market nottingham',datetime('now')),('Q26546814','The Thurland Hall','The Thurland Hall|Thurland Hall',52.953765,-1.146316,'GB','pub',1900,22.85,'Thurland Hall','the thurland hall grade ii listed public house in nottingham pub the thurland hall is a grade ii listed public house in nottingham',datetime('now')),('Q26547384','Whitelock''s Ale House','Whitelock''s Ale House',53.79721,-1.543378,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Whitelock''s Ale House','whitelock''s ale house pub in leeds west yorkshire england uk pub whitelock''s ale house is a pub in the city centre of leeds in england the pub lies on turk''s head yard on a narrow burgage plot off briggate',datetime('now')),('Q26547462','Scarbrough Hotel','Scarbrough Hotel|Scarbrough Hotel w Leeds',53.795361,-1.546298,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,NULL,'scarbrough hotel pub in leeds west yorkshire england uk pub hotel',datetime('now')),('Q26547491','The Golden Beam','The Golden Beam',53.816911,-1.570945,'GB','pub',1912,22.85,'The Golden Beam','the golden beam pub in headingley leeds west yorkshire england uk pub the golden beam is a pub and grade ii listed building located in the headingley area of leeds west yorkshire england it was built in c',datetime('now')),('Q26547879','The Red Lion','The Red Lion',53.957257,-1.077729,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Red Lion, York','the red lion pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the red lion is a grade ii listed pub on walmgate in the city centre of york england it is claimed that it is the oldest building in the city used as a pub however it has only been licensed since the 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26547958','The Mount Public House','The Mount Public House',53.953922,-1.09423,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Mount, York (pub)','the mount public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the mount is a grade ii listed public house on the mount in york england the present building is dated to around 1870 with its frontage described in the listing as later 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26547974','Cross Keys Hotel','Cross Keys Hotel',53.940461,-1.106663,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Cross Keys, Dringhouses','cross keys hotel hotel in york north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the cross keys is a grade ii listed public house on tadcaster road in dringhouses a suburb of york england an inn has occupied the site since around 1250 and the present building originated as an early 18th century hotel that was altered and expanded over the following two centuries',datetime('now')),('Q26547982','The Corner Pin','The Corner Pin',53.958494,-1.08687,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Corner Pin','the corner pin pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the corner pin is a grade ii listed public house on tanner row in york england the building originated as a mid 18th century house and was later adapted for use as an inn trading as the unicorn by 1804 under successive owners and licensees',datetime('now')),('Q26547994','Ye Olde Starre Inne','Ye Olde Starre Inne',53.961248,-1.083615,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Ye Olde Starre Inne','ye olde starre inne pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub ye olde starre inne is a historic public house on stonegate in the city centre of york england the main block of the pub is a timber-framed structure constructed in the 16th century and a wing to its left was added in about 1600',datetime('now')),('Q26548027','The Punch Bowl Public House','The Punch Bowl Public House',53.960557,-1.083744,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Punch Bowl, Stonegate','the punch bowl public house grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the punch bowl is a public house on stonegate in the city centre of york england the business was founded in 1675 as a coffeehouse and it became associated with the city''s whigs who preferred to drink punch',datetime('now')),('Q26548186','The Three Cranes Public House','The Three Cranes Public House',53.959875,-1.081588,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Three Cranes','the three cranes public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the three cranes is a grade ii listed public house on st sampson''s square in york england built in the mid 18th century it was altered in the late 19th century and refurbished in 1933',datetime('now')),('Q26548236','Harkers','Harkers',53.960196,-1.084858,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Harkers, York','harkers grade ii listed pub in york england uk pub harkers is a public house in the city centre of york england built in 1847 as the headquarters of the yorkshire insurance company to a design by george townsend andrews it stands on st helen''s square at its corner with lendal',datetime('now')),('Q26548478','The Other Tap And Spile Public House','The Other Tap And Spile Public House',53.958132,-1.085682,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Yorkshire Hussar','the other tap and spile public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the yorkshire hussar is a grade ii listed former public house on north street in york england a pub on the site was known as the yorkshire hussar from around 1840 and the present building constructed in 1896 to designs by walter green penty continued to use that name until about 1980',datetime('now'));
