ents in a row of seven constructed in the mid-14th century probably before 1369',datetime('now')),('Q26548672','Nags Head, York','Nags Head, York|The Nags Head',53.956899,-1.0897,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Nags Head, York','nags head york pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the nags head is a grade ii listed public house on micklegate in york england the building originated as a house with a front range added around 1530 to a 14th century rear range and was extended about 1700 by the mid 18th century it was operating as the nag''s head inn',datetime('now')),('Q26548732','19, Market Street','19, Market Street',53.958727,-1.081979,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'19 Market Street','19 market street building in york north yorkshire england uk pub 19 market street is a grade ii listed former public house on market street in york england established as a mid 19th century pub it was trading as the tiger by 1983 and remained in use as licensed premises until the early 1990s when it briefly traded as the william bass',datetime('now')),('Q26548735','The Burns Hotel','The Burns Hotel',53.958698,-1.08169,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Burns Hotel','the burns hotel pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the burns hotel is a grade ii listed public house on market street in york england it is formed from a mid 19th century pub and an adjoining early 18th century house that once stood as a pair with no',datetime('now')),('Q26548823','Number 26 And The Lendal Cellars Public House','Number 26 And The Lendal Cellars Public House',53.95994,-1.085473,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Lendal Cellars','number 26 and the lendal cellars public house grade ii listed public house in york north yorkshire england uk pub lendal cellars is a grade ii listed public house reached from a passageway off lendal in york england the building incorporates late 17th and mid 18th century cellars and stands on stone footings thought to be remnants of the late-13th-century augustinian friary that occupied the site until the dissolution',datetime('now')),('Q26548846','Rose and Crown, York','Rose and Crown, York|Rose & Crown',53.955054,-1.069533,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Rose and Crown, York','rose and crown york pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the rose and crown is a grade ii listed public house restaurant and bed-and-breakfast on lawrence street in york england it occupies two early 18th century houses later altered in the 19th and 20th centuries and the earliest known reference to the pub dates from 1786',datetime('now')),('Q26548847','The Waggon And Horses Public House (Number 19)','The Waggon And Horses Public House (Number 19)',53.954947,-1.069229,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Waggon and Horses','the waggon and horses public house number 19 pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the waggon and horses is a grade ii listed public house and bed and breakfast on lawrence street in york england built in 1773 as a house now no',datetime('now')),('Q26548870','The Kings Arms Public House','The Kings Arms Public House',53.957162,-1.083019,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Kings Arms, York','the kings arms public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the kings arms is a public house standing by the river ouse in the city centre of york england the building lies across king''s staith from the river at its corner with king street',datetime('now')),('Q26548882','The Fox','The Fox',53.95536,-1.106253,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Fox, York','the fox grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub inn the fox is a public house on holgate road in holgate a suburb of york england the pub was purpose-built in 1878 replacing an earlier establishment on the site',datetime('now')),('Q26548932','The Crystal Palace Public House','The Crystal Palace Public House',53.953932,-1.096775,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Crystal Palace, York','the crystal palace public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the crystal palace is a grade ii listed public house on holgate road in york england built around 1845 to 1850 and named after the structure created for the 1851 great exhibition it lies within the central historic core conservation area and remains in use today as a samuel smith''s establishment',datetime('now')),('Q26549042','The Old White Swan Public House','The Old White Swan Public House',53.960655,-1.080214,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Old White Swan','the old white swan public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the old white swan is a historic public house in the city centre of york england the core of the building is timber-framed and was constructed in the early 17th century',datetime('now')),('Q26549063','The Cross Keys','The Cross Keys',53.961802,-1.079902,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Cross Keys, York','the cross keys pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the cross keys is a grade ii listed public house on the corner of goodramgate and deangate in york england an inn on the site is recorded from 1783 and the present building was completed in 1904 to designs by frank raney for c j melrose and co replacing an earlier structure demolished during the creation of deangate',datetime('now')),('Q26549100','The Phoenix Public House','The Phoenix Public House',53.954153,-1.075039,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Phoenix Inn','the phoenix public house grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the phoenix inn is a grade ii listed public house on george street in york england standing just inside the city walls the building is variously dated to the late 18th or early 19th century and was remodelled in 1897 for john smith''s brewery to designs by bromet & thorman of tadcaster',datetime('now')),('Q26549158','The Edinburgh Arms','The Edinburgh Arms',53.953027,-1.075917,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Edinburgh Arms','the edinburgh arms grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the edinburgh arms is a historic public house on fishergate in york england the building was constructed in about 1830 when fishergate the street leading south out of the city centre was built up',datetime('now')),('Q26549176','Sea Horse Hotel','Sea Horse Hotel',53.953332,-1.075834,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Sea Horse Hotel','sea horse hotel grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the sea horse hotel is a grade ii listed public house and bed and breakfast on fawcett street in york england the building dates from the mid 19th century and the site was included within the newly established central historic core conservation area in 1968',datetime('now')),('Q26549177','The Woolpack Public House','The Woolpack Public House',53.953134,-1.075747,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Woolpack, York','the woolpack public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the woolpack is a grade ii listed former public house on fawcett street in york england built as a house around 1845 and converted into a pub in the 20th century the site was included within the central historic core conservation area in 1968',datetime('now')),('Q26549243','The Three Tuns','The Three Tuns',53.957721,-1.080904,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Three Tuns','the three tuns grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the three tuns is a public house on coppergate in the city centre of york england the building was probably constructed in the 16th century and is timber-framed with the first floor jettied',datetime('now')),('Q26549298','The Last Drop Inn','The Last Drop Inn',53.959968,-1.079635,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'27 Colliergate','the last drop inn pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub 27 colliergate now trading as the last drop inn is a grade ii listed public house on colliergate in york england built as a late 16th century house it was enlarged in the 17th and early 18th centuries including a brick front added around 1725 and a major rear extension and was modernised in the 20th century with a new shopfront',datetime('now')),('Q26549755','The Ship Public House','The Ship Public House',54.277436,-0.412352,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Ship, Scarborough','the ship public house pub in scarborough north yorkshire england uk pub the ship is a historic pub in scarborough north yorkshire a town in england the pub was originally built in the 18th or 19th centuries with the roof dating from the 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26550338','The Burton Stone Inn','The Burton Stone Inn',53.967233,-1.092981,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Burton Stone Inn','the burton stone inn grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the burton stone inn is a grade ii listed public house and bed-and-breakfast on clifton in the suburb of clifton in york england an inn on the site is first recorded in 1828 originally named the plough before later taking the name the burton stone after the medieval cross base that stands beside the building',datetime('now')),('Q26550346','The Old Grey Mare Public House','The Old Grey Mare Public House',53.968966,-1.096343,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Old Grey Mare, York','the old grey mare public house pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the old grey mare is a grade ii listed public house on clifton green in clifton a suburb of york england dating from the late 17th century it is thought to stand on the site of an earlier inn the maypole which was reportedly destroyed by fire in 1648',datetime('now')),('Q26550457','Blue Boar','Blue Boar',53.957423,-1.081245,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Blue Boar, York','blue boar grade ii listed pub in york england uk pub the blue boar is a public house on castlegate in the city centre of york england the blue boar was a medieval inn on the street',datetime('now')),('Q26550583','Exhibition Hotel','Exhibition Hotel',53.963249,-1.085583,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Exhibition, York','exhibition hotel grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub the exhibition is a public house on bootham a street leading north from the city centre of york england the building was constructed in the late 18th century as a large house',datetime('now')),('Q26550607','Bay Horse Inn','Bay Horse Inn',53.95412,-1.093159,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Bay Horse, Blossom Street','bay horse inn inn in york north yorkshire england uk inn the bay horse is a public house on blossom street immediately west of the city centre of york england the core of the building was constructed in the late 17th century after the siege of york as a small farmhouse',datetime('now')),('Q26550631','The Punch Bowl','The Punch Bowl',53.955533,-1.090903,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Punch Bowl, Blossom Street','the punch bowl grade ii listed pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub hotel building the punch bowl is a grade ii listed public house on the corner of blossom street and nunnery lane in york england it was formed from adjoining buildings dating from about 1835 and 1863',datetime('now')),('Q26550632','Windmill Hotel','Windmill Hotel',53.955473,-1.091675,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Windmill Inn','windmill hotel pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the windmill inn is a public house on blossom street immediately west of the city centre of york england the oldest part of the pub stands on the corner of blossom street and queen street although until 1911 another building separated it from queen street',datetime('now')),('Q26550642','The Wellington Inn','The Wellington Inn',53.947292,-1.077004,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Wellington Inn','the wellington inn pub in york north yorkshire england uk pub inn the wellington inn is a grade ii listed public house on alma terrace in york england dating from around 1850 it is a mid terrace back street pub a short walk from the river ouse and was designated in 1994 as part of a joint campaign for real ale camra and english heritage pilot study on historic pub interiors',datetime('now')),('Q26551611','White Swan Hotel','White Swan Hotel',54.245892,-0.777229,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The White Swan Inn, Pickering','white swan hotel hotel in pickering ryedale north yorkshire england uk pub hotel the white swan inn is a historic pub in pickering north yorkshire a town in england the pub was built in the 18th century on the site of a mediaeval building of which some passages and a door survive in the basement',datetime('now')),('Q26552763','The George and Dragon','The George and Dragon',53.496179,-2.519104,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'George and Dragon, Leigh','the george and dragon grade ii listed pub in leigh greater manchester england uk pub the george and dragon is a grade ii listed public house on king street in leigh a town within the metropolitan borough of wigan greater manchester england built in the mid-17th century it was later altered in the 19th and 20th centuries although the nature of those works was not recorded',datetime('now')),('Q26558796','The Duke Of Sussex Public House','The Duke Of Sussex Public House',51.496306,-0.264111,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Duke of Sussex, Acton Green','the duke of sussex public house pub in ealing london england uk pub the duke of sussex acton green is a public house opened in 1898 in the northern chiswick district of acton green it is prominently situated on a corner facing the common',datetime('now')),('Q26559218','The White Horse Public House','The White Horse Public House',51.794298,-0.079993,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The White Horse, Hertford','the white horse public house pub in hertford east hertfordshire england uk pub the white horse is a public house on the south side of castle street hertford england the pub occupies numbers 31 and 33 castle street two of a group of three grade ii listed houses that also includes number 35',datetime('now')),('Q26560563','Red Lion Inn','Red Lion Inn',53.431363,-2.229125,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Red Lion, Withington','red lion inn pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub inn the red lion officially listed as the red lion inn is a grade ii listed public house on wilmslow road in withington a suburb of manchester england dating from the 17th century it is thought to be the oldest surviving building in the suburb having begun as a farmhouse or possibly a small group of cottages before later operating as an inn',datetime('now')),('Q26561082','Plymouth Grove Hotel','Plymouth Grove Hotel',53.464695,-2.223234,'GB','pub|restaurant',NULL,13.17,'Plymouth Grove Hotel','plymouth grove hotel hotel in manchester greater manchester england uk restaurant pub hotel the plymouth grove hotel is a grade ii listed former hotel and public house on plymouth grove in chorlton-on-medlock an inner city area of manchester england built in the early 1870s and later incorporated into the boddingtons brewery estate it closed in 2003 and remained derelict for more than a decade before reopening as a restaurant in 2016',datetime('now')),('Q26561099','The Brunswick Hotel','The Brunswick Hotel',53.479983,-2.233186,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Brunswick Hotel, Manchester','the brunswick hotel pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub hotel the brunswick hotel now trading as the brunswick is a grade ii listed public house at the corner of piccadilly and paton street manchester england built in the early 19th century the property originally comprised a hotel with two adjoining townhouses which were later combined and adapted for use as licensed premises',datetime('now')),('Q26561231','Cross Daggers','Cross Daggers',53.358372,-1.369775,'GB','restaurant',NULL,13.17,'Cross Daggers','cross daggers restaurant in sheffield south yorkshire england uk restaurant the cross daggers is a restaurant and former pub in woodhouse sheffield england the building overlooks the village stocks as well as the cross',datetime('now')),('Q26561403','The City Public House','The City Public House',53.484414,-2.233374,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The City, Manchester','the city public house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the city is a grade ii listed former public house on oldham street in the northern quarter area of manchester england the building originated as two dwellings constructed before 1782 and 