ed by the standish community forum claims the present building was erected around 1450 and refers to earlier use by travellers and later as a coaching inn',datetime('now')),('Q26576016','The Ellesmere Public House','The Ellesmere Public House',53.518651,-2.396989,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Ellesmere','the ellesmere public house grade ii listed pub in walkden salford greater manchester england uk pub the ellesmere is a grade ii listed former public house on walkden road in walkden a town in the city of salford greater manchester england built in the 1860s or 1870s in a high victorian gothic style it stood beside walkden stocks station and was built to serve its passengers',datetime('now')),('Q26576855','The Old Crown Inn','The Old Crown Inn',51.403519,-2.43219,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Old Crown, Kelston','the old crown inn inn in kelston bath and north east somerset somerset england uk inn the old crown is a pub in kelston somerset it is featured in the good beer guide by the campaign for real ale and is cask marque accredited',datetime('now')),('Q26579421','The Green Man','The Green Man',54.134865,-0.800003,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Green Man, Malton','the green man pub in malton ryedale north yorkshire england uk pub the green man is a historic former pub in malton north yorkshire a town in england the pub originated as three buildings on market street in the town centre',datetime('now')),('Q26579522','Cott Inn','Cott Inn',50.442348,-3.708584,'GB','pub',1601,16.17,'Cott Inn','cott inn thatched pub in dartington south hams devon england uk thatched pub the cott inn is a medieval inn at dartington devon in the southwest of england founded in 1307 it is the second oldest inn in britain and a listed building',datetime('now')),('Q26581020','Peveril Of The Peak Public House','Peveril Of The Peak Public House',53.474959,-2.244655,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Peveril of the Peak, Manchester','peveril of the peak public house pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub