af is a historic building in garstang lancashire england built in the late 18th century it has been designated a grade ii listed building by historic england',datetime('now')),('Q26604444','The Green Tree','The Green Tree',54.311255,-1.665506,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Green Tree','the green tree pub in patrick brompton richmondshire north yorkshire england uk pub the green tree is a historic pub in patrick brompton a village in north yorkshire in england the building was constructed as a house in the mid 18th century and is said to have at one time served as the vicarage',datetime('now')),('Q26604482','Street Head Inn','Street Head Inn',54.269406,-2.004541,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Street Head Inn','street head inn inn in newbiggin richmondshire north yorkshire england uk inn the street head inn is a historic pub in newbiggin a village near aysgarth in north yorkshire in england the coaching inn was built in about 1730',datetime('now')),('Q26604486','The George Inn','The George Inn',54.276785,-2.001041,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The George Inn, Thoralby','the george inn pub in thoralby richmondshire north yorkshire england uk pub inn the george inn is a historic pub in thoralby north yorkshire england',datetime('now')),('Q26607754','The Three Guineas','The Three Guineas',51.45876,-0.97224,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Three Guineas, Reading','the three guineas grade ii listed pub at reading railway station reading uk pub the three guineas is a grade ii listed public house located at reading railway station in reading england it occupies a building originally built in or before 1867',datetime('now')),('Q2660945','Berndlalm','Berndlalm',47.1853,12.2597,'AT','pub',NULL,13.17,NULL,'berndlalm building in neukirchen salzburg austria mountain hut mountain pasture inn',datetime('now')),('Q26609470','The Chequers Inn','The Chequers Inn',51.149449,0.687064,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Chequers Inn, Smarden','the chequers inn pub in smarden ashford kent england uk pub inn the chequers inn is a public house in the village of smarden in kent it has been listed grade ii on the national heritage list for england since february 1967',datetime('now')),('Q2661513','Belle-Vue Brewery','Belle-Vue Brewery|Brouwerij Belle Vue|ベルビュー・ブルワリー|Brasserie Belle-Vue|cervecería Belle-Vue|Brauerei Belle-Vue|Belle-Vue',50.798817,4.287111,'BE','brewery',1913,37.07,'Belle-Vue Brewery','belle-vue brewery brewery in zuun belgium lambic brewery brewery belle-vue brewery is a brewery founded in 1913 in molenbeek brussels by philémon vandenstock from nearby itterbeek which lies in a region known for its lambic type of beer a variety of belle-vue lambic and fruit beers are produced in sint-pieters-leeuw',datetime('now')),('Q2661716','Va Doux Vent','Va Doux Vent',50.812333,4.342483,'BE','restaurant',NULL,12.0,NULL,'va doux vent restaurant in uccle belgium restaurant french cuisine',datetime('now')),('Q26619322','The Peacock Inn','The Peacock Inn',53.235223,-1.430254,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Peacock Inn, Chesterfield','the peacock inn inn in chesterfield derbyshire england uk inn the peacock inn is a grade-ii listed building located on low pavement in chesterfield derbyshire',datetime('now')),('Q26625709','Coach And Horses Public House','Coach And Horses Public House',51.894226,-1.757997,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Coach and Horses, Bourton-on-the-Water','coach and horses public house pub in bourton-on-the-water cotswold gloucestershire england uk pub the coach and horses is a public house on the a429 stow road fosse way near bourton-on-the-water a village in gloucestershire england it stands on a plot of 1 25 acres 0 51 ha and has a floorspace of 3 652 square feet 339 3 m2',datetime('now')),('Q26626866','Old Windmill Inn','Old Windmill Inn',52.40821,-1.517858,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Old Windmill','old windmill inn historic public house coventry england pub inn the old windmill is a public house in spon street in coventry england it is a grade ii listed 15th-century building with a history going back to around 1451 when it constructed around the trunk of a tree',datetime('now')),('Q26629770','Station Hotel','Station Hotel',53.387268,-2.348743,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Station Hotel, Altrincham','station hotel hotel in trafford greater manchester england uk pub hotel the station hotel is a grade ii listed public house on stamford new road in altrincham a market town within trafford greater manchester england built in the late 19th century it was operating as a pub by the 1930s',datetime('now')),('Q26629771','Lord Nelson Hotel','Lord Nelson Hotel',53.536828,-2.575353,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Lord Nelson Hotel, Hindley','lord nelson hotel pub in hindley wigan greater manchester england uk pub hotel the lord nelson hotel is a grade ii listed public house on bridge street in hindley a town within the metropolitan borough of wigan greater manchester england built in the late 18th century it was altered in the mid-19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26629933','The Rose And Crown Public House','The Rose And Crown Public House',53.846103,-0.437262,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Rose & Crown, Beverley','the rose and crown public house pub in beverley east riding of yorkshire england uk pub the rose & crown is a historic pub in beverley a town in the east riding of yorkshire in england the pub was built in about 1900',datetime('now')),('Q26630154','Bell Hotel','Bell Hotel',54.005677,-0.439774,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Bell Hotel, Driffield','bell hotel hotel in driffield east riding of yorkshire england uk pub hotel the bell hotel is a historic building in driffield a town in the east riding of yorkshire in england the building operated as an inn and shop in the 18th century and from 1772 housed the town''s first post office',datetime('now')),('Q26630155','Tiger Inn','Tiger Inn',54.004705,-0.438284,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Tiger Inn, Driffield','tiger inn pub in driffield east riding of yorkshire england uk pub inn the tiger inn is a historic pub in driffield a town in the east riding of yorkshire in england the pub lies on the east side of the market place',datetime('now')),('Q26630421','The Green Man Public House','The Green Man Public House',51.698611,-0.174875,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Green Man, Potters Bar','the green man public house pub in potters bar uk pub the green man is a disused public house in high street potters bar england and a grade ii listed building with historic england it was built in the mid 17th century and subsequently remodelled and extended',datetime('now')),('Q26630424','The White Hart Public House','The White Hart Public House',51.696854,-0.23342,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The White Hart, South Mimms','the white hart public house pub in south mimms hertsmere hertfordshire england uk pub the white hart is a grade ii listed public house in south mimms hertfordshire england',datetime('now')),('Q26630624','The Fleur De Lis Public House','The Fleur De Lis Public House',51.751454,-0.340772,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Fleur de Lys, St Albans','the fleur de lis public house pub in st albans hertfordshire england uk pub the fleur de lys or lis was a public house in french row st albans hertfordshire england the building has an c18th brick facade but it dates from the middle ages and is listed grade ii with historic england',datetime('now')),('Q26631528','The Beehive Public House','The Beehive Public House',51.785866,-0.187898,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Beehive, Welwyn Garden City','the beehive public house pub in welwyn garden city hertfordshire england uk pub the beehive is a grade ii listed public house in beehive lane welwyn garden city in hertfordshire the building dates from around the early seventeenth century',datetime('now')),('Q26631554','The Wrestlers Public House','The Wrestlers Public House',51.770334,-0.216537,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Wrestlers, Hatfield','the wrestlers public house pub in hatfield welwyn hatfield hertfordshire england uk pub the wrestlers is a public house on the great north road in hatfield hertfordshire england the grade ii listed building has an eighteenth-century chequered red brick front but it is based on a sixteenth-century core which preserves some of its timber framing',datetime('now')),('Q26631577','The Hope and Anchor Public House','The Hope and Anchor Public House',51.733214,-0.217709,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Hope and Anchor, Welham Green','the hope and anchor public house pub in north mymms welwyn hatfield hertfordshire england uk pub the hope and anchor was a grade ii listed public house in welham green hertfordshire it is based on a 17th-century timber frame with later additions',datetime('now')),('Q2663364','Brauhaus Stüsser','Brauhaus Stüsser|Neusser Straße 47 (Köln)',50.953,6.95704,'DE','beer_hall',NULL,13.17,NULL,'brauhaus stüsser german restaurant brewpub',datetime('now')),('Q26633840','Kings Arms Public House','Kings Arms Public House|The Black Rat',51.05796,-1.306886,'GB','pub|restaurant',NULL,13.17,'Black Rat (restaurant)','kings arms public house pub in winchester hampshire england uk restaurant pub the black rat was a restaurant in winchester in hampshire england as of 2021 the restaurant lost its one star in the michelin guide that had been held since 2011',datetime('now')),('Q2663524','Bon-bon','Bon-bon',50.82285,4.446347,'BE','restaurant',NULL,19.02,NULL,'bon-bon restaurant in belgium restaurant french cuisine',datetime('now')),('Q26637947','The Ship Inn','The Ship Inn',50.083333,-5.317167,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Ship Inn, Porthleven','the ship inn pub in porthleven cornwall england uk inn the ship inn is a grade ii listed public house in porthleven cornwall england dating to around 1805 it stands on mount pleasant road overlooking porthleven harbour from its western side',datetime('now')),('Q26638946','Colliers Arms Public House','Colliers Arms Public House',53.56127,-2.598587,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Colliers Arms, Aspull','colliers arms public house pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the colliers arms is a grade ii listed public house on wigan road in aspull a village within the metropolitan borough of wigan greater manchester england built in 1700 a date also recorded on a datestone it reopened in november 2023 after refurbishment work',datetime('now')),('Q26639043','Cross Keys Public House','Cross Keys Public House',53.55308,-1.988671,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Cross Keys Inn, Uppermill','cross keys public house grade ii listed pub in uppermill saddleworth oldham greater manchester ol3 pub the cross keys inn is a grade ii listed public house on running hill gate in uppermill a village in saddleworth within the metropolitan borough of oldham greater manchester england built in 1745 and first opened as an inn in 1763 it was formerly known as the gravemakers',datetime('now')),('Q26639057','The Swan Inn','The Swan Inn',53.556369,-2.012989,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Swan Inn, Dobcross','the swan inn grade ii listed public house in dobcross saddleworth oldham greater manchester ol3 pub inn the swan inn is a grade ii listed public house on the square in dobcross a village in saddleworth within the metropolitan borough of oldham greater manchester england built in 1765 as indicated by a datestone the building''s upstairs room was used as a magistrates'' court in the 18th century',datetime('now')),('Q26639077','The Grapes','The Grapes',53.541834,-2.0685,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Grapes Inn, Lees','the grapes pub in lees oldham greater manchester england uk pub the grapes inn now trading as the grapes is a grade ii listed public house on st john street in lees a town within the metropolitan borough of oldham greater manchester england built in 1741 but having undergone alterations and additions since then it has functioned as a pub for more than two centuries and remains in operation today',datetime('now'));
INSERT INTO institutions VALUES ('Q26639084','White Hart Public House','White Hart Public House',53.535851,-2.041483,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'White Hart, Lydgate','white hart public house grade ii listed pub in lydgate saddleworth oldham greater manchester england uk pub hotel the white hart is a grade ii listed public house on stockport road in lydgate a village in saddleworth within the metropolitan borough of oldham greater manchester england built in the 1790s although some sources give a more precise date of 1788 it was originally a house and may have served as a weavers'' cottage before its later conversion to a pub',datetime('now')),('Q26639350','The Hare and Hounds Public House','The Hare and Hounds Public House',53.547903,-2.005727,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Hare and Hounds, Uppermill','the hare and hounds public house grade ii listed pub in uppermill saddleworth oldham greater manchester england uk pub the hare and hounds is a grade ii listed public house on high street in uppermill a village within the metropolitan borough of oldham greater manchester england built in the late 18th century it has remained a presence in the village centre for more than two hundred years',datetime('now')),('Q26639358','White Lion Public House','White Lion Public House',53.569077,-2.023593,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'White Lion, Delph','white lion public house grade ii listed public house in delph saddleworth oldham greater manchester england uk pub the white lion is a grade ii listed public house on delph lane in delph a village in saddleworth within the metropolitan borough of oldham greater manchester england built in the mid to late 18th century it originated as three separate houses and was in use as an inn by the late 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q26643830','The Old Ship','The Old Ship',53.928568,-2.909733,'GB','restaurant',NULL,13.17,'The Olde Ship','the old ship building in pilling lancashire england uk restaurant house the olde ship is a historic building in pilling lancashire england it was built in 1782 for sea captain and slave trader george dickinson 1732 1806 and has been designated a grade ii listed building by historic england',datetime('now')),('Q26643873','Royal Oak Hotel','Royal Oak Hotel',53.899892,-2.774633,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Royal Oak Hotel, Garstang','royal oak hotel hotel in garstang wyre lancashire england uk pub hotel the royal oak hotel is a public house and hotel the market place of garstang lancashire england a grade ii listed building the pub is owned by robinsons brewery',datetime('now')),('Q26644171','The Inn at Whitewell','The Inn at Whitewell',53.91719,-2.520432,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Whitewell Hotel','the inn at whitewell grade ii listed hotel in the parish of bowland forest low ribble valley lancashire england uk inn hotel whitewell hotel is an historic building in the english parish of bowland forest low lancashire it is grade ii listed built in 1836 and is in sandstone with a slate roof in two storeys with attics',datetime('now')),('Q26653217','The White Horse Public House','The White Horse Public House',51.834325,-0.169422,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The White Horse, Burnham Green','the white horse public house pub in datchworth east hertfordshire england uk pub the white horse is a grade ii listed public house in whitehorse lane burnham green in the parish of datchworth in hertfordshire the building dates from around the seventeenth century',datetime('now')),('Q26656398','Colliers Arms Public House','Colliers Arms Public House',53.520312,-2.058873,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Colliers Arms, Mossley','colliers arms public house pub in mossley tameside greater manchester england uk pub the colliers arms is a grade ii listed former public house on lily lanes on the outskirts of mossley a town in tameside greater manchester england built in the late 18th century as a house and altered in the 19th century it stands on the hillside below hartshead pike tower',datetime('now')),('Q26660154','Hare and Hounds','Hare and Hounds',53.485072,-2.237863,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Hare and Hounds, Shudehill','hare and hounds pub in manchester greater manchester england uk pub the hare and hounds is a grade ii listed public house on shudehill in manchester england built around 1800 it is one of the city centre''s oldest surviving pubs and is rated by the campaign for real ale with three stars for having an interior of outstanding national historic importance',datetime('now')),('Q26661176','The Prince Albert Public House','The Prince Albert Public House',50.828476,-0.140665,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Prince Albert, Brighton','the prince albert public house pub in brighton and hove england uk pub the prince albert is a pub and music venue in trafalgar street brighton england built in 1848 it was originally a three-storey town house and converted to a pub in 1860',datetime('now')),('Q26664300','John Bull Chophouse','John Bull Chophouse',53.546101,-2.631107,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'John Bull Chophouse','john bull chophouse grade ii listed pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the john bull chophouse is a grade ii listed public house on coopers row in wigan greater manchester england thought to date from the 17th or early 18th century it was possibly formed from two cottages and a stable and is also recorded as having served as a slaughterhouse at an unknown date',datetime('now')),('Q26664307','The Pagefield Hotel','The Pagefield Hotel',53.552444,-2.643548,'GB','pub',NULL,12.0,'Pagefield Hotel','the pagefield hotel hotel in wigan greater manchester england uk pub hotel the pagefield hotel also known as the famous pagefield is a grade ii listed former public house on gidlow lane in wigan greater manchester england built in 1902 for the bolton brewery magee marshall & co and designed by heaton ralph and heaton it is noted for its interior which the campaign for real ale camra rates as of special national historic importance',datetime('now')),('Q26664346','The Springfield Public House','The Springfield Public House',53.554093,-2.647845,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Springfield Hotel','the springfield public house grade ii listed pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the springfield hotel officially listed as the springfield public house is a grade ii listed public house on springfield road in wigan greater manchester england built in 1903 for oldfield brewery to designs by the local architects heaton and ralph it retains a largely intact interior which is recognised by the campaign for real ale camra with a three star rating for its outstanding national historic importance',datetime('now')),('Q26664349','The Whitesmiths Arms','The Whitesmiths Arms',53.549499,-2.629361,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Whitesmiths Arms','the whitesmiths arms pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the whitesmiths arms is a grade ii listed public house on standishgate in wigan greater manchester england believed to date from the late 17th century it is the oldest surviving burgage plot building in wigan and among the oldest properties in the town centre',datetime('now')),('Q26664352','Royal Oak Hotel','Royal Oak Hotel',53.550134,-2.628359,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Royal Oak, Wigan','royal oak hotel grade ii listed pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the royal oak officially listed as the royal oak hotel is a grade ii listed public house on standishgate in wigan greater manchester england thought to date from the mid to late 18th century it was later extended and altered',datetime('now')),('Q26664370','The Raven Hotel','The Raven Hotel',53.54563,-2.631809,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Raven Hotel','the raven hotel grade ii listed pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the raven hotel currently trading as the raven is a grade ii listed public house on wallgate in wigan greater manchester england built in 1904 to designs by heaton ralph and heaton as a replacement for an earlier pub of the same name it retains a number of original interior features recognised in its listing',datetime('now')),('Q26664374','Dog and Partridge','Dog and Partridge',53.545554,-2.632593,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Dog and Partridge','dog and partridge grade ii listed pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the dog and partridge officially listed simply as public house is a grade ii listed public house on wallgate in wigan greater manchester england built in the late 18th or early 19th century the pub has traded under several names including the reported early name dog and partridge later the bees knees and last orders before ultimately reverting to its original name',datetime('now')),('Q26664375','The Berkeley','The Berkeley',53.545018,-2.632056,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Berkeley, Wigan','the berkeley pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the berkeley officially listed as 27 and 29 wallgate including 2 4 and 6 king street is a grade ii listed public house on wallgate in wigan greater manchester england built around 1820 as an inn it was long known as the minorca hotel and was remodelled in 1857 to designs by alfred waterhouse with further alterations in 1968',datetime('now')),('Q26664379','The Clarence Hotel','The Clarence Hotel',53.545068,-2.632782,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Clarence Hotel, Wigan','the clarence hotel hotel in wigan greater manchester england uk pub hotel the clarence hotel which currently trades as harry''s bar is a grade ii listed public house on wallgate in wigan greater manchester england built in 1898 and designed by w e v crompton it has served both as a hotel and a pub and is closely associated with the world pie eating championship which has usually been held there since its establishment in 1992',datetime('now')),('Q26664383','Swan and Railway Hotel','Swan and Railway Hotel',53.54392,-2.633957,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Swan and Railway Hotel','swan and railway hotel grade ii listed pub in wigan greater manchester england uk pub the swan and railway hotel is a grade ii listed public house on wallgate in wigan greater manchester england built in 1898 for walkers of warrington to designs by w e v crompton it was first operated as a hotel before later trading mainly as a pub and now functions as both',datetime('now')),('Q26665836','Black Friar Public House','Black Friar Public House',53.486521,-2.25349,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Black Friar, Salford','black friar public house pub in salford greater manchester england uk pub the black friar is a grade ii listed public house on blackfriars road in salford england built in 1886 in a vernacular revival style for henry boddington ii and attributed to the manchester architect william ball it replaced the old school inn on king street after the creation of blackfriars road in the 1880s',datetime('now')),('Q26665839','The Crown Tavern','The Crown Tavern',53.484069,-2.248713,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Crown, Salford','the crown tavern pub in salford greater manchester england uk pub hotel the crown is a grade ii listed former public house on blackfriars street in salford england built in the early 19th century it gained a tiled frontage in the late 19th century with crown hotel set into the tilework',datetime('now')),('Q26665842','The Kings Arms','The Kings Arms',53.484125,-2.255962,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'King''s Arms, Salford','the kings arms pub in salford uk pub the king''s arms is a grade ii listed public house on bloom street in salford england built in 1879 in a gothic style it replaced an earlier king''s arms that stood on the opposite side of the road and was licensed from 1807',datetime('now')),('Q26665851','Maypole Public House','Maypole Public House',53.492879,-2.28414,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Maypole, Salford','maypole public house pub in salford greater manchester england uk pub the maypole is a grade ii listed former public house on broughton road in pendleton an inner-city district of salford england built in around 1860 in a gothic style it was designed by the manchester architect james redford and originally opened as a hotel named after a maypole that stood beside the site',datetime('now')),('Q26665867','The Punch Bowl Public House','The Punch Bowl Public House',53.484578,-2.250118,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Punch Bowl, Salford','the punch bowl public house pub in salford greater manchester england uk pub the punch bowl officially listed as no 81 chapel street and no',datetime('now')),('Q26665914','19, 20 And 21, The Crescent','19, 20 And 21, The Crescent',53.482949,-2.266951,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Crescent (pub)','19 20 and 21 the crescent building in salford greater manchester england uk pub the crescent officially listed as 19 20 and 21 the crescent is a grade ii listed former public house on crescent a6 in salford england built in the early 19th century as a terrace of three houses and later combined and converted into a pub it is associated in local tradition with visits by karl marx and friedrich engels',datetime('now')),('Q26667213','The Ship Public House','The Ship Public House',54.584976,-0.96512,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Ship, Saltburn-by-the-Sea','the ship public house pub in saltburn marske and new marske redcar and cleveland north yorkshire england uk pub the ship is a historic public house on saltburn road in saltburn-by-the-sea a seaside town in redcar and cleveland england the pub dates from the late 18th century and is the oldest in saltburn having formed part of the original fishing village before the later town was developed on the opposite side of skelton beck following the arrival of the railways',datetime('now')),('Q26667377','Bath Hotel','Bath Hotel',53.379191,-1.482257,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Bath Hotel, Sheffield','bath hotel pub in sheffield south yorkshire england uk pub the bath hotel is a pub in broomhall district of sheffield in england the building was built in about 1868 as a grocers'' shop at the end of a terrace of houses on victoria street',datetime('now')),('Q26667500','The Bay Mare','The Bay Mare',53.603225,-2.432646,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Bay Mare','the bay mare pub in bolton greater manchester england uk pub the bay mare is a grade ii listed public house on blackburn road in astley bridge an area of bolton greater manchester england built around 1830 it occupies part of a listed terrace arranged along blackburn road and pemberton street',datetime('now')),('Q26667512','Maxims','Maxims',53.579156,-2.427189,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'26–28 Bradshawgate','maxims building in bolton greater manchester england uk pub 26 28 bradshawgate is a grade ii listed building on bradshawgate in bolton greater manchester england built in 1907 and originally operating as the fleece hotel it later traded under several names including the gaiety maxims and the flying flute public house before being converted into three commercial premises with flats on the upper floors in the late 2010s',datetime('now')),('Q26667522','Yates Wine Lodge','Yates Wine Lodge',53.578904,-2.427051,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Yates Wine Lodge, Bolton','yates wine lodge pub in bolton greater manchester england uk pub yates wine lodge is a grade ii listed former public house on bradshawgate in bolton greater manchester england built in 1906 it operated for more than a century and was most recently run as a branch of the yates''s pub chain before closing in 2025',datetime('now')),('Q26667545','The Finishers Arms','The Finishers Arms',53.591586,-2.468075,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Finishers Arms','the finishers arms pub in bolton greater manchester england uk pub the finishers arms is a grade ii listed public house on church road in bolton greater manchester england built around 1830 it incorporates an adjoining house from a later phase of development',datetime('now')),('Q26667550','The Swan Hotel','The Swan Hotel',53.579392,-2.426421,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Swan Hotel, Bolton','the swan hotel hotel in bolton greater manchester england uk pub hotel the swan hotel currently trading as the swan and barristers is a grade ii listed public house at the corner of churchgate and bradshawgate in bolton greater manchester england according to its official listing the building developed in four main phases between about 1800 and around 1900 with possible remnants of an earlier structure while the campaign for real ale camra gives a construction date of 1845',datetime('now')),('Q26667619','Stork Tavern','Stork Tavern',53.595883,-2.449176,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Stork Tavern','stork tavern pub in bolton greater manchester england uk pub the stork tavern is a grade ii listed public house on halliwell road in halliwell an area of bolton greater manchester england built around 1850 the site includes a former bowling green to the rear',datetime('now')),('Q26667652','Kings Head Public House','Kings Head Public House',53.568168,-2.466609,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'King''s Head, Bolton','kings head public house pub in bolton greater manchester england uk pub the king''s head is a grade ii listed public house on junction road in deane an area of bolton greater manchester england built in the late 18th century and extended in the mid-19th century it stands within the deane village conservation area and has continued to operate as a pub into the 21st century',datetime('now')),('Q26667672','Churchills Public House','Churchills Public House',53.570522,-2.420956,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Churchills, Bolton','churchills public house pub in bolton greater manchester england uk pub churchills formerly the rose hill is a grade ii listed former public house on manchester road in great lever a suburb of bolton greater manchester england built in the early 19th century it closed in 2009 and has since suffered arson damage the building remains derelict and as of september 2026 no proposals for its reuse have been recorded',datetime('now')),('Q26670454','Brewery Tap','Brewery Tap',51.456957,-0.192903,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Ram Inn, Wandsworth','brewery tap pub in wandsworth london pub the ram inn also known as the brewery tap which was its name for much of the later twentieth century is a historic pub at 68 wandsworth high street wandsworth london sw18',datetime('now')),('Q26671476','Swan With Two Necks Public House','Swan With Two Necks Public House',53.412034,-2.160662,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Swan with Two Necks, Stockport','swan with two necks public house grade ii listed pub in stockport greater manchester england uk pub the swan with two necks is a grade ii listed public house on princes street in stockport greater manchester england a pub has occupied the site since about 1830 and the present building dates from the 1920s or early 1930s following its acquisition and subsequent rebuilding by robinsons brewery which still owns it',datetime('now')),('Q26671900','Eagle Inn And Attached Dwelling','Eagle Inn And Attached Dwelling',53.487295,-2.251149,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Eagle Inn','eagle inn and attached dwelling pub in salford greater manchester england uk pub the eagle inn is a grade ii listed public house on collier street in salford england dated 1902 and built in an edwardian baroque style it is rated by the campaign for real ale camra for having an interior of special national historic importance',datetime('now')),('Q26672585','The Sale','The Sale',53.417389,-2.311381,'GB','pub',1878,16.17,'The Sale (pub)','the sale pub in sale trafford greater manchester england uk pub hotel the sale is a grade ii listed public house on marsland road in brooklands an area of sale within trafford greater manchester england built in 1878 as the moorfield hotel to designs by lockwood smith and heathcote it originally formed part of the moorfields estate created after the closure of the adjoining sale botanic gardens',datetime('now'));
