preserved to the present day in only a few pubs',datetime('now')),('Q27083453','Queen Adelaide','Queen Adelaide|The Queen Adelaide',51.506611,-0.237502,'GB','pub',NULL,19.85,'The Queen Adelaide','queen adelaide pub in shepherd''s bush london pub the queen adelaide is a pub at 412 uxbridge road shepherd''s bush london w12 it is a greene king property',datetime('now')),('Q27083738','The Harrow','The Harrow|The Harrow (Londres)',51.51298,-0.106784,'GB','pub',NULL,19.85,'The Harrow, London','the harrow pub in the city of london pub the harrow is a pub at 22 whitefriars street london it is a grade ii listed building built in the early 18th century and was originally two houses',datetime('now')),('Q27083820','The Bell','The Bell|The Bell (Cidade de Londres)',51.51101,-0.089443,'GB','pub',NULL,19.85,'The Bell, City of London','the bell pub in city of london england uk pub the bell is a public house at 29 bush lane in the city london ec4 it is a grade ii listed building probably built in the mid 19th century',datetime('now')),('Q27083993','Green Man Public House','Green Man Public House',51.515563,-0.136757,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'The Green Man, Soho','green man public house pub in westminster london england uk pub the green man is a grade ii listed public house at 57 berwick street in london''s soho',datetime('now')),('Q27084059','The Ferry Boat Inn','The Ferry Boat Inn',51.586948,-0.052524,'GB','pub',NULL,13.17,'Ferry Boat Inn, Walthamstow','the ferry boat inn pub in waltham forest london england uk pub inn the ferry boat inn is a public house situated on the east bank of the river lea on ferry lane walthamstow in the london borough of waltham forest the oldest parts of the building date from the early 18th century and it is a grade ii listed building first registered by the municipal borough of walthamstow in 1951',datetime('now')),('Q27084186','Percy Arms Public House','Percy Arms Public House|Percy Arms',51.529323,-0.112999,'GB','pub',NULL,12.0,'Percy Arms','percy arms 